# SCENARIO: fix_124_debug_isolation   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: none   BOTCFG: auto
# Fix #124 - `reload debug,<names>` gives a quiet world: non-debug bots are despawned and kept out by
# the engine (debugisolate), and pinned debug bots take no self-initiated actions (no PK/vigilante/
# gang/reroll/idle-teleport) while still defending themselves. A plain `reload` ENDS debug mode.
# Run: runner.py fix_124_debug_isolation.steps --var D1="<bot A>" --var D2="<bot B>"
#   (two Thais bots, e.g. the baseline's Thunker Ashwing + Shymm Dawnsbane). The scenario performs
#   the debug reload itself and ALWAYS cleans up: the runner stops early only on a STUCK verb or an
#   infra error, so every client verb before the cleanup is optional=1 (a failed expect does not stop
#   the run). Restart canary afterwards: leaving debug mode does not repopulate (BOT_SYSTEM_DOCS.md).
# Baseline (2026-11-18, bl_b4/bl_b5): non-target bots woke and ran AI under debug mode
#   ("Woke bot 'Ed Amberwind' ... reason=proximity", "[HuntAssign] Montegue Ragerunner -> ...",
#   "KITE Montegue Ragerunner ... reason=max_legs", 246 PROCBOT_SLOW for Ed Amberwind) and a pinned
#   bot went "Thunker Ashwing IDLE->PK_ATTACK".
# Acceptance (server truth):
#   - `debugisolate status` reports ON with pinned=2 active=2 right after the reload, and still
#     active=2 after the player has stood in Thais for 120 s;
#   - zero `[DEBUG_ISOLATE] despawned ... (tick sweep)` lines (the backstop never has to act);
#   - zero audit `wake result=ok` and zero audit `state` transitions for any bot other than D1/D2;
#   - census `active` is 2 in every census record of the window;
#   - D2 (never attacked, a white-skulled player beside it) never enters COMBAT or PK_ATTACK;
#   - D1 may react to the player's attack (self-defense is kept by design), but never PK_ATTACK;
#   - a plain `reload` during debug mode ENDS it: "debug mode ENDED by plain reload" in the journal
#     and `debugisolate status` = OFF pinned=0 afterwards;
#   - after the final `reload debug off`, isolation is still OFF.
# The pinned-PvP part is UNDERPOWERED by nature (vigilante is a 5% roll per newly seen PKer); the
# gate itself is deterministic code, so 0 transitions is the expected, not a lucky, outcome.
@srv cmd _global "reload debug,$D1;$D2"
@srv sleep 20
@srv cmd _global debugisolate status expect="ON pinned=2 active=2"
@srv audit kinds state,wake,cmd,census
@srv audit watch *
@srv audit on expect="enabled=on"
@srv audit mark "F124 start"
@srv cmd "$D1" teleport 32369,32215,7
@srv cmd "$D2" teleport 32371,32213,7
@p1 login optional=1
@p1 goto 32369,32217,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=120 optional=1
@srv audit mark "F124 poke D1 (white skull for the player)"
@p1 attack $D1 optional=1
@p1 hold 6 optional=1
@p1 attack stop optional=1
@p1 login optional=1
@p1 goto 32371,32216,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=90 optional=1
@p1 hold 120 watch=$D1,$D2 optional=1
@srv audit mark "F124 end"
@srv cmd _global debugisolate status expect="ON pinned=2 active=2"
@srv expect-none src=srv k=debug_isolate msg~="tick sweep" within=300
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=wake result=ok name~="^(?!($D1|$D2)$)" within=300
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=state name~="^(?!($D1|$D2)$)" within=300
@srv expect src=srv:audit k=census active=2 min=1 within=300
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=census active~="^(?!2$)" within=300
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=state bot=$D2 to~="COMBAT|PK_ATTACK" within=300
@srv expect-none src=srv:audit k=state bot=$D1 to=PK_ATTACK within=300
@srv audit watch clear
@srv audit off
@p1 logout optional=1
# ---- a plain reload ends debug mode (and is the first half of the cleanup) ----
@srv cmd _global reload
@srv sleep 20
@srv expect src=srv msg~="debug mode ENDED by plain reload" min=1 within=40
@srv cmd _global debugisolate status expect="OFF pinned=0"
# ---- cleanup (NOT optional): clears the persisted debug count too ----
@srv cmd _global "reload debug off"
@srv sleep 20
@srv cmd _global debugisolate status expect="OFF"
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=600
@p1 note "debug mode is off; it does not repopulate: restart canary after this scenario"
